Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[N 26-26 Call of Water]
[D Forever Shaman 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Shaman only: the rest of Call of Water in one trip from the Blackfathom hearth - Stonewatch Falls, Hervdana's cave, Astranaar and back, Norric, the Forgotten Shrine in Westfall - ending in Ironforge with the Water Totem and Mana Spring Totem trained.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffCall of Water in one trip|r  -  you stand at Sentinel Hill after the Blackfathom hearth with Call of Water (94499) in the log. Six hand-ins, 7,495 quest XP and the Water Totem, plus Knowledge in the Deeps (2,750 XP) handed in at the end; about 75 minutes, most of it birds, boats and running. The quests need level 20; the chapter sits at 26 because Mana Spring Totem is a level-26 spell. Hearth = Sentinel Hill and it stays there
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00What you need:|r the flight paths of Lakeshire, Thelsamar, Menethil Harbor, Auberdine and Astranaar (chapters 06-12) and silver for the trainer at the end (Mana Spring Totem alone is 40s). The only fight the chain asks for is one level-22 elemental
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Red Waterskin already full?|r Chapter 10 fills it at Stonewatch Falls. If yours is full, skip the Redridge block by hand and fly from Thor to Thelsamar

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffRedridge: Stonewatch Falls|r  -  the falls are in the east, 10 units south of the Tower of Ilgalar. Stonewatch Keep (x 60-66, y 52-60) is all elites: stay on the road north of it. The Shadowhide gnolls on the east road are 22-26 and Morganth's tower (75.0,49.5) is thick with them: the statue lies east of it, walk south from there
[A Shaman] At [TAR523 Thor], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Lakeshire]|r [G56.5,52.6 Westfall]
[A Shaman] Take the road east along the north shore, past the watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep (58.2,49.8), to the Old Lion Statue [G79.4,46.8 Redridge Mountains]
[A Shaman] Walk south to the foot of Stonewatch Falls beside the Murloc Nightcrawlers (level 21-22) and use the [UI265747 Unfilled Red Waterskin] there [QC94499] [G76.1,59.6 Redridge Mountains]
[OC][A Shaman] The DB has no object for the falls; the quest text puts it near the Nightcrawlers, whose only spawns are here. Rohh the Silent (a level 26 rare) also has spawn points in this corner - leave him
[A Shaman] Run back to Lakeshire and at [TAR931 Ariena Stormfeather], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r (the game routes it through Stormwind and Ironforge) [G25.5,59.4 Redridge Mountains]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffWetlands: Hervdana, first visit|r  -  Dun Algaz again (Dragonmaw orcs, level 19-21), then east to the cave under the southern falls. |cffffcc00Golm|r, a level 32 ELITE elemental: the DB (QuestieDB 1.1.1) lists 79 positions for him, 46 of them inside x64-69, y66-75.5 - the nearest is one unit north of the cave mouth. The quest that kills him wakes him with a Goaz Stone, so he may stand dormant until then (unverified). Look before you cross the last stretch, come in from the south-west along the south edge, and if he is up and close to the door, wait until he has moved north
[A Shaman] From Thelsamar run up the west road to the north exit at Mountaineer Rockgar [G25.4,10.4 Loch Modan]
[A Shaman] Through Dun Algaz to where the pass opens into the Wetlands [G48.6,76.0 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] East to [TAR258203 Hervdana Saegrund] in her cave, [QT94499] (1,300 XP) [QA94500 Call of Water] (the Blue Waterskin is for the lake at Astranaar) [G65.8,76.4 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] Run north-west to Menethil Harbor (about 60 units, 6 minutes; Ghost Wolf) and take the boat to Auberdine from the dock (the sign on the pier names the destination) [G8.3,59.1 Wetlands]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffAstranaar|r
[A Shaman] At flight master [TAR3841 Caylais Moonfeather], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Astranaar]|r [G36.3,45.6 Darkshore]
[A Shaman] Use the [UI265772 Unfilled Blue Waterskin] on the lake at the north tip of town, beside the flight master [QC94500] [G34.4,48.0 Ashenvale]
[OC][A Shaman] |cff66ff66Normal|r - one click. The quest says "the waters of Astranaar" and the skin's text says the body of water around the town; Classic-era sources put Astranaar on an island in a lake, so any shore works (the DB gives no exact spot)
[A Shaman] At [TAR4267 Daelyshia], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Auberdine]|r [G34.4,48.0 Ashenvale]
[A Shaman] Walk to the western dock and take the boat to Menethil Harbor; get off at Menethil (it carries on to Southshore) [G33.5,40.0 Darkshore]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffWetlands: Hervdana again, then Norric|r
[A Shaman] Run south-east past the Mosshide camps toward the cave; stay west of x 64 until you are south of y 76, then turn east to the cave (Golm's ground is x64-69, y66-75.5) [G60.4,70.9 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] At [TAR258203 Hervdana Saegrund], [QT94500] (1,400 XP) [QA94501 Call of Water] (the Vial of Purest Water goes to Norric Lochthane at the north end of Loch Modan) [G65.8,76.4 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] West to the pass and back through Dun Algaz into Loch Modan [G25.4,10.4 Loch Modan]
[A Shaman] At [TAR258043 Norric Lochthane] at the north end of the loch, [QT94501] (460 XP) [QA94502 Call of Water] (he gives you the Water Sapta, which lets you see elemental spirits) [G41.8,19.1 Loch Modan]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffWestfall: the Forgotten Shrine|r
[A Shaman] |cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Sentinel Hill]|r
[OC][A Shaman] If the Hearthstone is still cooling down from the Blackfathom hearth, run down the west road to Thelsamar (about 4 minutes) and fly to Sentinel Hill from Thorgrum Borrelson instead
[A Shaman] Walk south-west to Stendel's Pond and the Forgotten Shrine on its shore, drink the [UI6637 Water Sapta] at the shrine and kill the Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water you can now see (level 22), then loot the Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers [QC94502] [G45.6,59.9 Westfall]
[A Shaman] Hand the bracers in at the Forgotten Shrine, [QT94502] (1,400 XP) [QA94503 Call of Water] (the log text still says return to Norric; ignore it) - the pond glows and the Minor Manifestation of Water appears in it [G45.6,59.9 Westfall]
[A Shaman] Swim out to the [TAR5895 Minor Manifestation of Water] in the pond, [QT94503] (185 XP) [QA94505 Call of Water] (it hands you the Shard of Water, nothing to kill) [G47.5,60.4 Westfall]
[OC][A Shaman] The whole finale is in Westfall (Warcraft Tavern, played through); the Silverpine spawns in the DB (38.6,44.6) are the Horde chain's
[A Shaman] At [TAR523 Thor], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r (the game routes it through Stormwind and Ironforge) [G56.5,52.6 Westfall]
[A Shaman] Run up the west road to the north end of the loch (about 4 minutes) and at [TAR258043 Norric Lochthane], [QT94505] (2,750 XP) - the fixed reward is the |cff66ff66Water Totem|r. Keep it in your bags: every water totem needs it [G41.8,19.1 Loch Modan]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffIronforge: the trainer|r
[A Shaman] Back at [TAR1572 Thorgrum Borrelson], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Ironforge]|r [G33.9,51 Loch Modan]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Water totems from the lower rows|r, when gold is easy: Poison Cleansing Totem (level 22, 30s) and Frost Resistance Totem (level 24, 35s). Healing Stream Totem rank 1 is not on Eldrun's list in the data - look for it now that you hold the totem
[A Shaman] In the Forlorn Cavern at [TAR258098 Eldrun Stormbreaker], [T] train |cff66ff66Mana Spring Totem|r (level 26, 40s) first, then the rest of your level 24 and 26 rows, which chapter 15 would otherwise buy (sheet: Rockbiter 4, Earth Shock 4, Lightning Shield 3 are musts, Strength of Earth 2 and Healing Wave 5 buys - 35s each; Magma Totem 40s; Lightning Bolt 5 (40s) when gold is easy; 2g 55s for the lot, against about 8g of quest money by now). Still 25? Buy the 24 row; chapter 15 comes back for the rest [G47.1,13.8 Ironforge]
[A Shaman] Two steps away at [TAR2786 Gerrig Bonegrip], [QT971] (2,750 XP) - |cffffcc00Gear:|r Sustaining Ring (+4 Sta, 4 health per 5 sec) only for an empty ring slot [G50.8,5.6 Ironforge]
[A Shaman] At [TAR1573 Gryth Thurden], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Sentinel Hill]|r [G55.5,47.7 Ironforge]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Check:|r Call of Water is finished, the Water Totem is in your bags and Knowledge in the Deeps (971) is handed in. Chapter 15's Ironforge hop is now optional for you. Next: walk from Sentinel Hill into Duskwood
[NX 25-26 Duskwood: Darkshire]
